    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1494">

                <pb facs="1126" n="1010" xml:id="pg1010"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.404/31a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Consuls in Mexico</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Identic telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-01-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 14, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In view of published reports of outrages upon nuns and priests and desecrations
                    of church property in Mexico, you are instructed to make report of any such
                    occurrences in your district since January 1, 1914, giving names, nationalities
                    and dates, and whether based on personal knowledge or reliable information.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
